ite `renderer.js` ```bash cat > renderer.js <<'EOF' const btn = document.getElementById("testBtn"); const output = document.getElementById("output"); btn.addEventListener("click", () => { output.textContent = "Button clicked. Renderer is working."; }); EOF ``` ### 6) Write `styles.css` ```bash cat > styles.css <<'EOF' body { margin: 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #111; color: #f5f5f5; } .app { padding: 40px; } button { padding: 10px 16px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer; } EOF ``` ### 7) Start it ```bash npm start ``` ## The blunt truth Nothing is broken right now. You just used the terminal wrong for the last step. - **Terminal commands** go in Bash - **JSON/JS/HTML/CSS** go into files If you want, next I’ll give you the **same setup as one single PowerShell script** so you can generate the whole Electron starter in one shot.
